# The project log is append-only: every row is a close-out, written once and
# never edited. Two branches that each close out a project conflict on the last
# line for no reason a human should have to read, so git keeps both rows.
#
# `union` is a built-in driver — no `git config` per clone, which matters
# because `mc run` merges inside worktrees it creates itself (`syncMain`,
# `src/mc/run.js`), where an installed driver would not be in force.
#
# The limit, and it is sharp: `union` keeps both sides of every conflicting
# hunk. That is right for a table only ever appended to and wrong the moment a
# row is edited, reordered or rewritten — the result is a silently duplicated
# row nobody notices. If you ever change an existing row in this file, this
# line stops being safe for that change. Nothing else in this repository gets
# `union`: every other conflict measured here was real content.
docs/project/project_log.md merge=union
